{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae0f-ee07-7b81-b4d4-cf94ccb5debd"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4"},"prompt":"# Agent Task Assignment\n\n## FIRST — Run Immediately\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'set_status(TASK-260830-3g12yp, status=reviewing)'\n```\n\n## Operational Constraints (Headless Run)\n\n- Never background a long command and end your turn: a headless session ends with\n  the turn and the process dies with it, while the run is still recorded as\n  completed with no evidence attached.\n- A single shell call is time-bounded (~10 minutes). Split long checks into\n  bounded sequential calls (package subsets, `-run` masks) and state explicitly\n  what you reran yourself versus accepted from already-attached evidence.\n- Attach evidence before you end the lifecycle, not after: \"I will attach it when\n  the run finishes\" is unfulfillable by construction.\n\nRun `task-board spawn directives \"$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID\"` at safe checkpoints,\nat most once per 1 minute, never in a loop.\nDirectives have no delivery timer.\nSave before cancel; pause/reroute safely.\nIf reading directives fails, report unknown; do not treat it as none.\n\n\n## Role Contract\n\n- **Role:** `reviewer` (`reviewer`) — Reviews implementation quality and project fit\n- Obey task scope, acceptance criteria, and checklist.\n- Report real exit codes; failing gates stay failing.\n- Use scoped board projections; skip `summary()`,\n  `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`. Request scoped schema only after an\n  unknown call.\n- Load only relevant and explicitly required skills.\n\n### Skills\n\n- `project-management`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/SKILL.md`\n- `architecture-diagrams`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Require winning lease and exact epoch before provider activation, input, mutation, checkpoint, or terminal restore\n- [ ] Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\n- [ ] README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\n- [ ] Code written per task description and AC\n- [ ] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\n- [ ] In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n- [ ] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\n- [ ] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n- [ ] Implementation matches AC\n- [ ] Solution fits project architecture\n- [ ] Tests green\n- [ ] Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\n- [ ] If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260830-3g12yp\n- **Title:** TASK-260830-3g12yp: implement-provider-and-pane-fencing-gates\n- **Parent:** STORY-260830-1oqfec\n\n### Description\n\nRequire winning lease and exact epoch before provider activation, input, mutation, checkpoint, or terminal restore. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\n\n### Scope\n\nrelux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); §2.2, §5.3, §13.6-13.10. Work only inside the ownership-leases-and-fencing story boundary.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nProduction behavior demonstrates: Require winning lease and exact epoch before provider activation, input, mutation, checkpoint, or terminal restore. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260830-3g12yp_producer.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-3g12yp/TASK-260830-3g12yp_producer.md`\n\n- Byte count: `6585`\n- Content digest: `sha256:12424d2d4e6fc14c4aedd57ae514c544aa1c0209493c77197bd42ed408f41672`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-3g12yp_reviewer-cr1.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-3g12yp/TASK-260830-3g12yp_reviewer-cr1.md`\n\n- Byte count: `5987`\n- Content digest: `sha256:1f3ada137cd44b7f20ee311f9cfe02a4d28e9f99b80fa6ac78290e63e983935a`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260830-3g12yp_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260830-3g12yp, name=TASK-260830-3g12yp_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- You are licensed to attempt to DEFEAT any gate, refusal, validation, authorization, or attestation under review, and to reject a change whose only evidence is positive-path. Grep for callers before believing a guard is in force; a delete-only mutant proves existence, not coverage.\n- Review read-only and record exactly one evidence-backed verdict: accepted → `done`; changes requested → `to-dev` or `analysis`; genuine Stop-The-Line → `blocked`. Never leave the task in `reviewing`.\n- With a `Change Request Under Review` section, accept via `task-board m 'accept_cr(ID, revision=N, evidence=ID_review-verdict.md)'`. It writes `accepted` and `integrating` atomically and routes the element to `integrating` — accepted work never stays in `reviewing` and never reaches `done` from here. The accepted revision is bound to its producer role and archetype; only a new tracked run with that exact producer role and archetype may checkpoint or integrate it, and the orchestrator routes that run but does not close the leaf. `accept_cr` takes no acknowledgement argument, and only the reviewer run that was handed the revision may call it.\n- Reviewer-archetype runs must not supply `commit_ack` and must not escalate the commit-or-acknowledge decision to the human; record acceptance evidence and leave every `done` transition to the producer side.\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260830-1oqfec.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-1oqfec`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED in the worktree — the handoff snapshots the working tree against the recorded checkpoint. A commit of your own on this branch is refused at handoff with `change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n\n## Change Request Under Review\n\n- Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-3g12yp-1` revision `1` (state `ready`)\n- Element: `TASK-260830-3g12yp`, integration scope: `STORY-260830-1oqfec`\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-1oqfec`\n- Base OID: `0ebb7faf656ebc9059d7f51f652fee08c680f8bf`\n- Candidate tree OID: `5c45354b667894a5fd434ffb0f8eddcf004244ff`\n- Repository delta: `present`\n- Patch resource: `TASK-260830-3g12yp_change-request_rev1.patch` (sha256 `c158c9f2b4de87b971d35efee1bcbe32a31bb8169c0997c497f9e904246b5fc3`)\n\n```bash\ngit -C . diff 0ebb7faf656ebc9059d7f51f652fee08c680f8bf 5c45354b667894a5fd434ffb0f8eddcf004244ff          # the exact reviewable delta\ngit -C . diff --stat 0ebb7faf656ebc9059d7f51f652fee08c680f8bf 5c45354b667894a5fd434ffb0f8eddcf004244ff   # its shape\n```\n\nChanged paths (22):\n\n- `LOGBOOK.md`\n- `README.md`\n- `internal/fencing/TRACEABILITY.md`\n- `internal/fencing/census_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/codes_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/doc.go`\n- `internal/fencing/fixtures_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/gate.go`\n- `internal/fencing/gate_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/scenarios_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/terminate.go`\n- `internal/fencing/terminate_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/testdata/forge/forge.go`\n- `internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py`\n- `internal/fencing/testdata/use/use.go`\n- `internal/fencing/token.go`\n- `internal/fencing/token_test.go`\n- `internal/sessquery/lease_store_adopt_test.go`\n- `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`\n- `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json`\n- `internal/traceability/traceability.go`\n- `internal/traceability/traceability_test.go`\n\n### Recording the verdict\n\nAcceptance is a named mutation, not a status change:\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'accept_cr(TASK-260830-3g12yp, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260830-3g12yp_review-verdict-rev1.md)'\n```\n\n`accept_cr` writes `accepted` and `integrating` atomically: the Change Request becomes `accepted`, this run is stamped as the reviewer, and TASK-260830-3g12yp routes the element to `integrating` — accepted but not landed, and never `done`. The accepted revision is bound to its producer role and archetype (`developer`/`implementer`), and only a new tracked run with that exact producer role and archetype may checkpoint or integrate it. The orchestrator routes that run; it does not close the leaf, and no orchestrator run may execute the integration itself. `done` is produced only by the integration transaction, never by you and never by an acknowledgement. Never supply `commit_ack` yourself.\n\nChanges requested and Stop-The-Line are unchanged: route to `to-dev`/`analysis` or evidence-backed `blocked`. Leaving the element in `reviewing` is still not a verdict and still gets this run cancelled and respawned.\n"}}
