{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae0f-ee07-7b81-b4d4-cf94ccb5debd"},"sequence":68,"recorded_at":1780531400000131,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae10049576419e1fbc08e35e286a","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-3g12yp/TASK-260830-3g12yp_producer.md`.\n1|Own TASK-260830-3g12yp (implement-provider-and-pane-fencing-gates), second leaf of STORY-260830-1oqfec (ownership-leases-and-fencing). Predecessor TASK-260830-2f5393 (internal/sessrepo lease_store.go: CreateLease, CompareAndSwapLease, GetLease/ListLeases/WinningLease, VerifyFencingToken, CheckFencingExpiry, CompareLeaseTuple agreeing with sessstate.Compare, grant-expiry-only policy, immutable content-addressed lease blobs, AfterLeaseStage crash seam) is accepted and checkpointed on the Story branch; sibling TASK-260830-2atgj4 (ownership reducer property tests) follows you. Implement the fencing gates the pinned v0.6.0 headings require — internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md Section 2.2 Global invariants (the winning committed lease is the only authority that may create a destination runtime; a fencing token is the winning lease_id + epoch pair carried by every owner-authored event and mutation; force takeover fences the prior owner logically), Section 5.3 Lease Record (epoch/predecessor/holder/fencing token), Sections 13.6-13.10 (graceful takeover, force takeover, fork, stop, resume: which steps require the winning lease and the exact epoch, what a losing/stale/unfenced token may never do, old-owner reconnect rejected with its lower/losing token, deterministic winner with losing history preserved) and the Section 4 terminal wrapper rule (\"compare the local fencing token before launching a provider; park safely when ownership is remote, ambiguous, or unverified\"; stale_fenced state; terminate-stale only for explicit force recovery) plus the Provider Protocol LeaseToken {session_id, lease_epoch, lease_id} carried by quiesce/capture/materialize operations (Section 7.5). Deliver as production code over the landed owners without a second model: a fencing gate package (for example internal/fencing) exposing typed, unforgeable gate checks that every activation-class action must pass — provider activation/launch, provider input (quiesce-input/attach direction), owner-authored mutation (event append, CAS), checkpoint capture (internal/sessckpt Capture/Admit already bind the owning lease tuple — reuse that admission), and terminal restore/wrapper first start — each check requiring (1) the winning lease per sessrepo.WinningLease/sessquery admission, (2) the exact epoch and lease_id equality with the presented token (a lower epoch, a losing lease_id at the same epoch, a token for a different session, an expired fencing grant per CheckFencingExpiry, or an absent/unverified ownership all refuse with the Section 15 classes lease_conflict exit 10 or the specific class the pinned text names — never a new class the taxonomy lacks), (3) a park decision (stale_fenced / parked with reason remote_owner|stale_owner|restore_policy|failed_handoff per the session.parked event vocabulary) instead of any launch when ownership is remote, ambiguous, or unverified; the LeaseToken projection for provider operations minted only from a passed gate (unforgeable: unexported fields, no exported constructor, minted by the gate only — the same sealed-capability discipline as the landed admittedCheckpoint/HeldExclusive tokens); refusal of terminate-stale outside explicit force recovery; and the old-owner-reconnect rejection. Do not implement the takeover/fork/stop/resume transactions or any terminal backend or provider plugin process; model them as callers and gate their entry points. Tests: drive each gate through its production entry with positives (winner, exact epoch) and the full refusal table (lower epoch, same-epoch loser, foreign session, expired grant, absent lease, ambiguous/remote ownership -> parked with the exact reason, unverified sync state), the old-owner-reconnect scenario after a force takeover (losing token rejected, divergent history preserved through sessstate union), concurrent force takeovers (deterministic winner), token forgery attempts (constructing a LeaseToken outside the gate must not compile or must be refused by a census gate you ship with executable controls — recall the landed sealed-capability censuses in sessquery and config), every gate a narrowing mutant (epoch compare >= instead of ==, lease_id prefix compare, expiry off-by-one, park-instead-of-refuse swapped) with a shipped harness and an applied harmless SURVIVED control, crash/idempotency evidence for any durable write you add (prefer none: gates are pure over durable inputs — if pure, state the bound explicitly), and a conformance matrix mapping each 2.2/5.3/13.6-13.10 fencing clause to a test or a stated bound. Story-close items you must carry (from the 2f5393 review verdict): update internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json section:5.3 (and add your fencing bindings) to the real production declarations with honest coverage text and re-pin reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 (precedent Stories 3drr2m, 3jqsx1, 3m2mw8, 2jylym); extend the CompareLeaseTuple/sessstate.Compare agreement test from 6 example pairs to an exhaustive small-alphabet enumeration (epochs {1,2,3} x holders {a,b} x lease ids {x,y} x created_at orderings) so any divergence is caught. README section for your package with test commands and no CLI/capability claim; LOGBOOK entry. Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-1oqfec whose tip is the 2f5393 checkpoint; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-3g12yp and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc). Evidence contract as in the repository DoD: production-entry tests with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites, negatives, narrowing mutants with per-plant raw logs and subprocess exits, conformance matrix, no unsupported claims. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff; hand off no later than 3.5 hours in. Attach TASK-260830-3g12yp_results.md, TASK-260830-3g12yp_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-3g12yp_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-3g12yp --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
