ethod value/reflection excluded by convention — say what the census covers), rerun TestLeaseTokenCensusPlants with your own plant shapes (an alias type, a composite literal through an unexported-field embedding, a var binding, a build-tagged file, a generic wrapper) and confirm the census refuses each; confirm the testdata/forge and testdata/use controls do what they claim. (5) Mutation — rerun testdata/mutate.py in an isolated copy, rerun each of the 31 KILLED twice, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on arms the producer did not mutate plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (6) Agreement — the exhaustive 144-pair enumeration must cover the full small alphabet (epochs {1,2,3} × lease IDs {x,y} × holders {a,b} per side); plant a tie-break divergence on each side and confirm it goes RED; confirm created_at is diagnostic-only per the pinned text. (7) Traceability and docs — the ownership registry changes (section:5.3 to CompareAndSwapLease 7/8 partial with clause 5.3#5 open, section:2.2 sliver 4/22 to Authorize, 9 acceptance cases, digest re-pin): recompute the projection digest independently, confirm every claimed clause line exists in the pinned document, confirm no self-minted claim (each binding names an existing production declaration with an acceptance case that drives it), tracecheck 28/485 reproduced; README figures/prose and LOGBOOK truthful, no CLI/capability claim; the residual section:17.2 nit correctly out of scope. (8) Hygiene — changed_paths exactly the candidate paths, no __pycache__/.pyc, no task-board.config.json, no stray plants; go vet, gofmt clean; go test ./internal/fencing ./internal/sessrepo ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessstate ./internal/traceability/... -count=1 and -race green; tracecheck and cataloggen -check exit 0 on the exact tree.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits,