{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c53d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae0f-ee07-7b81-b4d4-cf94ccb5debd"},"sequence":249,"recorded_at":1780531400000493,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae10-6366-7ef1-8edf-d44650a65eef"},"task_id":"01a0ae10-6366-7ef1-8edf-d44650a65eef","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae10-6366-7ef1-8edf-d44650a65eef","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-3g12yp/TASK-260830-3g12yp_conformance-matrix.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-3g12yp conformance matrix\n2|\n3|Authority: `relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec` v0.6.0, commit\n4|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`\n5|(`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`). Each row maps one fencing clause\n6|to the production entry and named test that discharges it, or to a\n7|stated bound. Line numbers are 1-based into `SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n8|\n9|## Section 2.2 Global invariants (lines 404-592)\n10|\n11|| Clause (ID) | Requirement | Disposition | Production call site | Named test(s) |\n12|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n13|| 2.2#1 (408) | Exactly one winning lease, hence one logical owner | Driven | `fencing.Observe` + `fencing.Authorize` | `TestObserveLoadsWinningLease`, `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations` |\n14|| 2.2#2 (410) | A replica MUST NOT launch, resume, accept input, or publish authoritative events | Driven | `fencing.Authorize*` (remote arm) | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/owner_resume_and_replica_park` |\n15|| 2.2#3 (412) | Every owner-authored event carries the winning epoch + lease ID | Driven | `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` | `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/graceful_takeover_commit` |\n16|| 2.2#4 (413) | Peers reject lower-epoch / losing same-epoch events, preserve divergent branch | Driven | `sessrepo.AppendEvent`, `sessstate.Projector.Project` | `TestAppendEventPreservesDivergentBranchWithoutApplying`, `TestAppendEventRefusesStaleLeaseEpoch`, `TestOldOwnerReconnectRejectedAfterForceTakeover/losing_events_preserved_without_application`, `/union_preserves_losing_branch` |\n17|| 2.2#5-#22 | Replication, secret, SQLite, materialization, tombstone, profile, capability, bridge, sync, continuation, readiness, exclusion, directory-merge preamble | Stated bound | — | No implementation in this ownership story; registry gap on `section:2.2` discloses each family. |\n18|\n19|## Section 5.3 Lease Record and ownership (lines 1908-1982)\n20|\n21|| Clause (ID) | Requirement | Disposition | Production call site | Named test(s) |\n22|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n23|| 5.3#1 (1927) | `created_by_host_id` MUST equal `issued_by_host_id` | Driven (predecessor) | `canonicaljson.validateLeaseRecord` | `core-record-identity-validation` case tests |\n24|| 5.3#2 (1957) | Epoch > 1 MUST name a known predecessor | Driven (predecessor + query) | `sessrepo.CompareAndSwapLease`, `sessquery.winningLeaseFor` | `TestCompareAndSwapPersistsSuccessor`, `TestSuccessorCycleMustRefuse`, `TestDanglingPredecessorMustRefuse`, `TestValidSuccessorBuildsAndRevalidates` |\n25|| 5.3#3 (1958) | Epoch MUST equal predecessor + 1 and reference a validated checkpoint | Driven (predecessor + query) | `sessrepo.CompareAndSwapLease`, `sessquery.winningLeaseFor` | `TestEpochMonotonicityAcrossSuccessors`, `TestSkippedEpochMustRefuse`, `TestWrongPredecessorCheckpointMustRefuse`, `TestWrongSessionCheckpointMustRefuse` |\n26|| 5.3#4 (1960) | Epoch-1 `create` MUST have a null predecessor | Driven (predecessor) | `sessrepo.CreateLease` | `TestCreateLeasePersistsEpochOneCreate`, `TestNormativeLeaseRecordExampleAttests` |\n27|| 5.3#5 (1962) | New takeover lease MUST use `max_observed_epoch + 1` | Stated bound | — | The union maximum is caller-side input; the store mints head + 1 and no takeover flow exists yet. Registry gap on `section:5.3` discloses it. |\n28|| 5.3#6 (1967), 5.3#7 (1968) | Losing/lower events preserved, never applied | Driven | `sessrepo.AppendEvent`, `sessstate.Reduce` | Same as 2.2#4, plus `TestWinnerResolutionLosingBranchPreserved`, `TestWinnerResolutionUnionSupersedesChain` |\n29|| 5.3#8 (1970) | Owner MUST revalidate before input, turn, checkpoint, push, resume | Driven | `sessrepo.VerifyFencingToken`, `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry`, `fencing.Authorize*` | `TestVerifyFencingTokenAcceptsWinner`, `TestVerifyFencingTokenRefusals`, `TestCheckFencingExpiry`, `TestAuthorizeRefusesExpiredGrant`, all `TestAuthorize*` refusal tables |\n30|\n31|## Sections 13.6-13.10 lifecycle fencing\n32|\n33|| Clause | Requirement | Disposition | Production call site | Named test(s) |\n34|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n35|| 13.6 step 10 | Destination creates epoch `source+1` after stop/prepare; MUST NOT adopt/resume under a concurrent winner | Driven (gate half) | `fencing.AuthorizeMutation`, `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/graceful_takeover_commit`; orchestration itself is a stated bound (modeled caller) |\n36|| 13.6 failure table | No failure before step 10 advances ownership; none after lets the source resume | Driven (gate half) | `fencing.Authorize*` | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesFailedHandoff`; orchestration is a stated bound |\n37|| 13.7 force lease | Only the winning committed force lease authorizes runtime creation; its token rejects the prior owner | Driven | `fencing.AuthorizeActivation`, `fencing.AuthorizeInput` | `TestOldOwnerReconnectRejectedAfterForceTakeover`, `TestAuthorizeEndToEndOverRepository` |\n38|| 13.7 old owner | Prior owner becomes stale; losing history preserved in divergent branches | Driv