{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c541","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae0f-ee07-7b81-b4d4-cf94ccb5debd"},"sequence":251,"recorded_at":1780531400000497,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae105f9771418b1d2ca2def6d454","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-3g12yp/TASK-260830-3g12yp_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-3g12yp results — implement provider and pane fencing gates\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the managed\n4|Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no commit was made on the Story\n5|branch.\n6|\n7|## Outcome\n8|\n9|`internal/fencing` gates every activation-class action on the winning\n10|lease and the exact fencing epoch: provider activation/launch,\n11|provider input, owner-authored mutation, checkpoint capture, and\n12|terminal restore/wrapper first start, plus terminate-stale under\n13|explicit force recovery. 18 of 18 AC rows are driven through\n14|production entries by named committed tests (0 of 18 as a public CLI,\n15|by stated ownership bound — no `ax` session command exists in this\n16|tree).\n17|\n18|AC coverage (row → production call site → named test):\n19|\n20|1. activation → `AuthorizeActivation` → `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestAuthorizeEndToEndOverRepository`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/fork_epoch_one_activation`\n21|2. input → `AuthorizeInput` → `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestOldOwnerReconnectRejectedAfterForceTakeover`, `TestConcurrentForceTakeoversDeterministicWinner`\n22|3. mutation → `AuthorizeMutation` → `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/graceful_takeover_commit`\n23|4. checkpoint → `AuthorizeCheckpoint` → `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/stop_checkpoint`\n24|5. restore → `AuthorizeRestore` → `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/owner_resume_and_replica_park`\n25|6. lower epoch → `Authorize` core → `TestAuthorizeRefusesLowerEpoch` (`stale_owner` / park `stale_owner`)\n26|7. same-epoch loser → `Authorize` core → `TestAuthorizeRefusesSameEpochLoser` (`lease_conflict` / park `stale_owner`)\n27|8. foreign session → `Authorize` core → `TestAuthorizeRefusesForeignSession` (`lease_conflict`)\n28|9. expired grant → `Authorize` core → `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry` → `TestAuthorizeRefusesExpiredGrant` (`lease_conflict`)\n29|10. absent lease → `Authorize` core + `Observe` → `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesAbsentWinner`, `TestObserveLoadsWinningLease` (park `restore_policy` / `lease_conflict`)\n30|11. ambiguity → `Authorize` core → `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesAmbiguous` (park `restore_policy` / `lease_conflict`)\n31|12. remote ownership → `Authorize` core → `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote` (park `remote_owner` / `not_owner`)\n32|13. unverified sync → `Authorize` core → `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesUnverified` (park `restore_policy` / `lease_conflict`)\n33|14. old-owner reconnect → `AuthorizeInput`/`AuthorizeMutation`/`AuthorizeRestore`/`AuthorizeActivation` + `Repository.AppendEvent` + `Projector.Project` → `TestOldOwnerReconnectRejectedAfterForceTakeover`\n34|15. concurrent takeovers → `CompareLeaseTuple`/`Compare` + `Authorize*` → `TestConcurrentForceTakeoversDeterministicWinner`\n35|16. forgery → `LeaseToken.Bind` + census → `TestBindRefusesForgedToken`, `TestLeaseTokenConstructorCensus`, `TestLeaseTokenCensusPlants`, `TestLeaseTokenUnforgeableOutsidePackage`\n36|17. terminate-stale → `AuthorizeTerminateStale` → `TestTerminateStale*` (8 tests)\n37|18. LeaseToken projection → `LeaseToken.Bind` → `TestBindProjectsMintedToken`, `TestBindRefusesUnknownOperation`, `TestMintedTokenIsStableAcrossEntries`\n38|\n39|## Negative evidence and mutants\n40|\n41|- Every gate arm ships a narrowing mutant: 30 N-mutants (epoch `==`\n42|  to `>=`/`<=`, lease/session/holder prefix confusion, expiry\n43|  widening, grant/clock carve-outs, park/refuse swaps) plus 1\n44|  token-preserving census-alias mutant executed against the full\n45|  behavioral suite (263 passing assertions alongside the census\n46|  failure). Battery result: 31/31 KILLED; the applied harmless\n47|  control is SURVIVED; the not-applied and compile-failure controls\n48|  classify separately. Harness:\n49|  `python3 internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py <evidence-dir>`.\n50|  Per-plant raw logs and `mutants.json` are under\n51|  `.temp/TASK-260830-3g12yp/mutants/` and inside the attached tarball.\n52|- No new error class is minted: `TestGateRefusalsUseRegisteredCodes`\n53|  constructs every sentinel through `internal/axerror` with its exact\n54|  exit (10/10/10/2/3), and every park unwraps to its Section 15 cause.\n55|- Crash/idempotency: the gates are pure (no durable writes), proven\n56|  by `TestGatesPerformNoDurableWrites` (byte-identical tree plus\n57|  identical verdicts across two runs). Stated bound, not a seam drill.\n58|\n59|## Traceability and agreement (story-close items)\n60|\n61|- `section:5.3` moved from the `canonicaljson` shape validator to the\n62|  real `CompareAndSwapLease` owner at 7/8 partial (only the\n63|  caller-side union-maximum clause 5.3#5 stays open, disclosed in the\n64|  gap); `section:2.2` moved from unowned to a 4/22 sliver bound to\n65|  `Authorize`; 9 lease acceptance cases registered\n66|  (`lease-record-lifecycle`, `lease-fencing-revalidation`,\n67|  `lease-checkpoint-admission`, `lease-divergent-preservation`,\n68|  `lease-union-resolution`, `lease-fencing-gates`,\n69|  `lease-fencing-park`, `lease-terminate-stale`,\n70|  `lease-token-capability`).\n71|- Pin re-derived: 110 acceptance cases, 57 bindings (full 1, partial\n72|  4, sliver 2, unevidenced 47, unmeasured 3), 11 unowned, 28/485\n73|  clauses; `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` updated and all\n74|  shipped-state tables (`tracecheck` pins, `Report` literal,\n75|  sliver-refusal rows, planted-sliver rows, README figures and\n76|  measured-coverage prose) moved deliberately.\n77|- `TestLeaseTupleOrderAgreesWithSessstateCompare` extended from 6\n78|  example pairs to an exhaustive 144-pair enumeration (epochs\n79|  {1,2,3} × lease IDs {x,y} × holders {a,b} per side, remaining\n80|  summary members varied); `created_at` takes no part in either\n81|  comparator (diagnostic-only per Section 5.3), disclosed in the\n82|  test comment.\n83|- Residual nit (out of scope, not changed): the `section:17.2` gap\n84|  rationale (\"no ownership implementation exists\") predates this\n85|  story; its measured coverage (0/1 unevidenced) is unchanged.\n86|\n87|## Validation (all run in this session, this worktree)\n88|\n89|- `go test ./internal/fencing/ -count=1` → ok (40 tests)\n90|- `go test ./internal/fencing/ -cover -count=1` → ok, 97.5%\n91|- `go test ./... -count=1` → exit 0, 27 packages ok, 0 FAIL\n92|- `go test -race` (fencing, sessrepo, sessquery, sessstate, traceability/...) → exit 0\n93|- `go vet ./...` and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` → clean\n94|- `go build ./...` and `GOOS=windows go build ./...` → clean\n95|- `gofmt -l internal` → empty (428 files scanned)\n96|- `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` → ok (110/57/28/485)\n97|- `python3 internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py` → exit 0, 31/31 KILLED\n98|- Full logs: `.temp/TASK-260830-3g12yp/full-test.log`,\n99|  `.temp/TASK-260830-3g12yp/race-touched.log`,\n100|  `.temp/TASK-260830-3g12yp/mutants/`\n101|\n102|## Files changed (uncommitted candidate)\n103|\n104|- New: `internal/fencing/{doc,gate,token,terminate}.go`,\n105|  `internal/fencing/{fixtures,gate,token,terminate,codes,census,scenarios}_test.go`,\n106|  `internal/fencing/testdata/{mutate.py,forge/forge.go,use/use.go}`,\n107|  `internal/fencing/TRACEABILITY.md`\n108|- Edited: `internal/sessquery/lease_store_adopt_test.go` (144-pair\n109|  enumeration), `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json`,\n110|  `internal/traceability/traceability.go` (pin),\n111|  `internal/traceability/traceability_test.go`,\n112|  `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`, `README.md`,\n113|  `LOGBOOK.md`\n114|\n115|## Bounds restated\n116|\n117|No `ax` command, doctor surface, or runtime capability is added or\n118|advertised; takeover/fork/stop/resume orchestration, terminal\n119|backends, and provider processes are modeled callers; no `sessckpt`\n120|package exists so `AuthorizeCheckpoint` is the capture admission;\n121|`resume`/`stop`/`materialize-commit`/`native-store-plan` bindings and\n122|clause 5.3#5 stay open as stated above. Full clause matrix:\n123|`TASK-260830-3g12yp_conformance-matrix.md`.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
