{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5e5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae0f-ee07-7b81-b4d4-cf94ccb5debd"},"sequence":333,"recorded_at":1780531400000661,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b7392d99-bbd5-4114-ba32-61509405cfc4"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae10-7a70-7ae0-b128-759d175d8eb6"},"task_id":"01a0ae10-7a70-7ae0-b128-759d175d8eb6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae10-7a70-7ae0-b128-759d175d8eb6","chunk":"Read text file `internal/fencing/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-3g12yp: implementation evidence\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.6.0, commit\n4|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`. Primary scope is Sections\n5|2.2, 5.3, and 13.6-13.10 (winning lease and exact epoch before\n6|provider activation, input, mutation, checkpoint, or terminal\n7|restore), the Section 4 terminal wrapper rule, and the Section 7.5\n8|`LeaseToken`. This file records implementation evidence; it changes no\n9|normative ownership and claims no public CLI delivery.\n10|\n11|The fencing gates (`internal/fencing`) require the winning lease and\n12|the exact epoch before every activation-class action. They mint no\n13|second lease model: the Lease Record lifecycle stays owned by\n14|`sessrepo` (`Observe` loads the winner through `ListLeases`, the\n15|expiry arm calls `CheckFencingExpiry`); the winning-tuple rule stays\n16|owned by `sessstate` (the gates compare one presented token for exact\n17|equality with the one winning summary and never order two leases);\n18|takeover, fork, stop, and resume transactions, terminal backends, and\n19|provider plugin processes are modeled as callers, not members.\n20|\n21|## Acceptance rows\n22|\n23|18 of 18 AC rows are driven at the production entries named below; 0\n24|of 18 are delivered as a public CLI surface, which is an explicit\n25|caller-integration bound (no `ax` session command exists in this\n26|tree), not a gap in the assigned shared behavior. Takeover/fork/stop/\n27|resume orchestration belongs to its owning leaves, which invoke these\n28|entries at every required boundary.\n29|\n30|| AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) | Evidence and bound |\n31|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n32|| Provider activation requires winner + exact epoch | `AuthorizeActivation` | `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestAuthorizeEndToEndOverRepository`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/fork_epoch_one_activation` | Driven: the winning lease with the exact epoch mints through the activation entry over pure and repository-backed observations, including the fork epoch-1 lease; a rival succession parks or refuses the old token. |\n33|| Provider input requires winner + exact epoch | `AuthorizeInput` | `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestOldOwnerReconnectRejectedAfterForceTakeover/new_owner_rejects_old_token_as_stale`, `TestConcurrentForceTakeoversDeterministicWinner` | Driven: exact input authorizes; the old token after a force takeover refuses `stale_owner`; the losing same-epoch token refuses `lease_conflict` once the union winner is known. |\n34|| Owner-authored mutation requires winner + exact epoch | `AuthorizeMutation` | `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/graceful_takeover_commit`, `TestAuthorizeEndToEndOverRepository` | Driven: the modeled graceful-takeover commit authorizes its mutation with the new winning tuple; the source token refuses after the succession. |\n35|| Checkpoint capture requires winner + exact epoch | `AuthorizeCheckpoint` | `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/stop_checkpoint` | Driven: the modeled stop checkpoint authorizes with the exact tuple and refuses `stale_owner` for a superseded token. No second checkpoint admission exists in this tree (the brief's `sessckpt` package is absent), so the gate is the capture admission (stated bound). |\n36|| Terminal restore requires winner + exact epoch | `AuthorizeRestore` | `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/owner_resume_and_replica_park` | Driven: the owner resume authorizes; the replica restore parks `remote_owner` with the `not_owner` cause instead of starting a runtime. |\n37|| Lower epoch refused | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeRefusesLowerEpoch` | Driven: a superseded epoch refuses `stale_owner` on input/mutation/checkpoint and parks `stale_owner` on activation/restore, for the standard old-lease vector and the winner-lease-at-lower-epoch vector. |\n38|| Same-epoch loser refused | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeRefusesSameEpochLoser` | Driven: a losing lease at the winning epoch refuses `lease_conflict` on input/mutation/checkpoint and parks `stale_owner` on activation/restore, for the standard and prefix-sharing losers. |\n39|| Foreign session refused | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeRefusesForeignSession` | Driven: a token for another session refuses `lease_conflict` on every entry, for the prefix-sharing and fully foreign sessions. |\n40|| Expired grant refused | `Authorize` via all five entries → `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry` | `TestAuthorizeRefusesExpiredGrant` | Driven: a lapsed grant refuses `lease_conflict` on every entry so the holder revalidates; a grant at exactly the boundary stays current; an unusable policy refuses `invalid_arguments`. Expiry logic is reused from the `sessrepo` owner, never restated. |\n41|| Absent lease parks or refuses | `Authorize` via all five entries; `Observe` | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesAbsentWinner`, `TestObserveLoadsWinningLease/no_leases_yields_no_winner` | Driven: with no winning lease, launch entries park `restore_policy` with an empty winning lease ID while the other entries refuse `lease_conflict`; `Observe` reports absence as data, never an error. |\n42|| Ambiguous ownership parks or refuses | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesAmbiguous` | Driven: conflicting union observations park `restore_policy` under the winner on launch entries and refuse `lease_conflict` elsewhere. |\n43|| Remote ownership parks or refuses | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote` | Driven: a remote winning holder parks `remote_owner` under the winner on launch entries and refuses `not_owner` elsewhere, for prefix-sharing and fully remote holders. |\n44|| Unverified sync parks or refuses | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesUnverified` | Driven: without a proving lease refresh, launch entries park `restore_policy` under the winner and the other entries refuse `lease_conflict`. |\n45|| Old-owner reconnect rejected, divergent history preserved | `AuthorizeInput`, `AuthorizeMutation`, `AuthorizeRestore`, `AuthorizeActivation`, `Repository.AppendEvent`, `sessstate.Projector.Project` | `TestOldOwnerReconnectRejectedAfterForceTakeover` | Driven: after a force takeover the old token refuses `stale_owner` from input/mutation/checkpoint on the new owner and parks `remote_owner` on the old wrapper; the losing event refuses stale with its bytes preserved and the chain untouched; the union projection reports `losing_branch_preserved` and `union_supersedes_chain` with authoritative state standing and the old-owner view stale. |\n46|| Concurrent force takeovers resolve deterministically | `sessrepo.CompareLeaseTuple`, `sessstate.Compare`, `AuthorizeInput`, `AuthorizeMutation`, `AuthorizeActivation` | `TestConcurrentForceTakeoversDeterministicWinner` | Driven: two same-epoch force leases from one base resolve to the greater lease ID in either union order under both tuple rules; the winner authorizes and the loser stops accepting input with `lease_conflict`. |\n47|| Token forgery refused | `LeaseToken.Bind`; constructor census | `TestBindRefusesForgedToken`, `TestLeaseTokenConstructorCensus`, `TestLeaseTokenCensusPlants`, `TestLeaseTokenUnforgeableOutsidePackage` | Driven: zero and field-assembled tokens refuse `lease_conflict` on every provider operation; only `token.go` names the seal types or assembles a non-empty token; comment/string mentions are not references while alias, direct, and shadowing forgeries are rejected; an outside package assembling the token by field name fails to build while the public-surface fixture builds. |\n48|| Terminate-stale outside force recovery refused | `AuthorizeTerminateStale` | `TestTerminateStaleAuthorizesFencedTarget`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutForce`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutDiagnostics`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutWinner`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesLiveOwner`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesForeignSession`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesMalformedTarget`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesGarbageWinner` | Driven: a fenced target (lower epoch, divergent, or beyond the winner) authorizes under explicit force recovery with preserved diagnostics; missing force, diagnostics, or winner, a live-owner target, a foreign session, and malformed members refuse their classes. |\n49|| LeaseToken bound to provider operations from a passed gate only | `LeaseToken.Bind` | `TestBindProjectsMintedToken`, `TestBindRefusesUnknownOperation`, `TestMintedTokenIsStableAcrossEntries` | Driven: a token minted by a passed gate projects the exact triple onto `quiesce`, `capture`, and `materialize` identically from every entry; unknown operations refuse `invalid_arguments`. Resume, stop, materialize-commit, and native-store-plan carry the same triple on the wire but have no gate entry here (stated bound). |\n50|\n51|## Refusal and recovery coverage\n52|\n53|Every `N-` row is a genuine narrowing mutant: the gate stays present\n54|and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must\n55|reject, and the named behavioral test fails through the delivered\n56|harness (`internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py`, run as\n57|`python3 internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py <evidence-dir>`).\n58|Whole-clause disables are not accepted as narrowing. The `T-` row\n59|preserves the searched-for `leaseSeal` token while constructing\n60|through an alias, and its harness run executes the full behavioral\n61|suite (263 passing assertions alongside the census failure), not only\n62|the static checker. Controls: `C-harmless-comment` is applied and\n63|survives, `C-not-applied` is not a kill, and `C-compile-failure`\n64|produces no named behavioral failure.\n65|\n66|| Gate | Named test | Narrowing mutant |\n67|| --- | --- | --- |\n68|| Operation enum | `TestAuthorizeRefusesUnknownOperation` | N-op admits exactly the bogus operation; the token authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n69|| Presented session grammar | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMalformedPresented/session_not_uuid` | N-presented-session admits exactly `not-a-uuid`; the refusal degrades to the foreign-session class. |\n70|| Presented epoch grammar | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMalformedPresented/epoch_zero` | N-presented-epoch admits exactly the epoch-zero winner-lease vector; the refusal degrades to the stale class. |\n71|| Presented lease grammar | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMalformedPresented/lease_not_uuid` | N-presented-lease admits exactly `zzz`; the refusal degrades to the loser class. |\n72|| Winner grammar | `TestAuthorizeRefusesGarbageWinner/epoch_zero_lease` | N-winner admits exactly the epoch-zero `zzz` winner; the refusal degrades to the ahead class. |\n73|| Session binding | `TestAuthorizeRefusesForeignSession/prefix_sharing` | N-session-prefix compares first UUID segments only; the prefix-sharing session authorizes while the fully foreign session still refuses. |\n74|| Winner absence | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesAbsentWinner/verified` | N-absent admits exactly the verified absence; the refusal degrades to the malformed-observation class. |\n75|| Sync verification | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesUnverified/unambiguous` | N-verified admits exactly the unambiguous unverified observation; the token authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n76|| Ambiguity | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesAmbiguous/verified` | N-ambiguous admits exactly the verified ambiguity; the token authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n77|| Handoff outcome | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesFailedHandoff/verified` | N-handoff admits exactly the verified failed handoff; the token authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n78|| Grant presence | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMissingGrant/verified` | N-grant admits exactly the verified grantless call; the refusal degrades to the lapsed-grant class. |\n79|| Clock presence | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMissingClock/zero_validated` | N-clock admits exactly the clockless never-validated grant; the token authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n80|| Grant expiry | `TestAuthorizeRefusesExpiredGrant/lapsed` | N-expiry extends the interval by an hour; the lapsed-by-seconds grant authorizes while the never-validated grant still refuses. |\n81|| Expiry classification | `TestAuthorizeRefusesExpiredGrant` | N-expiry-map swaps the lapsed/unusable classes; both vectors change class. |\n82|| Ownership direction | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote/prefix_sharing` | N-remote-prefix compares first UUID segments only; the prefix-sharing remote holder authorizes while the fully remote holder still refuses. |\n83|| Epoch equality, ahead side | `TestAuthorizeRefusesEpochBeyondWinner/exact_lease` | N-epoch-gte weakens `==` to `>=`; the ahead token authorizes while the lower-epoch vectors still refuse stale in the same run. |\n84|| Epoch equality, lower side | `TestAuthorizeRefusesLowerEpoch/exact_lease` | N-epoch-lte weakens `==` to `<=`; the lower token authorizes past the epoch arm while the ahead vectors still refuse in the same run. |\n85|| Lease equality | `TestAuthorizeRefusesSameEpochLoser/standard` | N-lease-vector admits exactly the standard loser; the prefix-sharing loser still refuses. |\n86|| Lease equality, prefix confusion | `TestAuthorizeRefusesSameEpochLoser/prefix_sharing` | N-lease-prefix compares first UUID segments only; the prefix-sharing loser authorizes while the standard loser still refuses. |\n87|| Launch classification, input side | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote/input` | N-launch-add-input parks input instead of refusing; the hard-refusal assertion fails. |\n88|| Launch classification, restore side | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote/restore` | N-launch-drop-restore refuses restore instead of parking; the park assertion fails. |\n89|| Capability seal | `TestBindRefusesForgedToken` | N-bind-seal admits exactly the field-assembled seal; the zero token still refuses. |\n90|| Provider operation enum | `TestBindRefusesUnknownOperation` | N-bind-op admits exactly the bogus operation; the projection mints and the negative fails by success. |\n91|| Terminate target grammar | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesMalformedTarget/lease_not_uuid` | N-term-presented admits exactly `zzz`; the termination authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n92|| Terminate winner grammar | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesGarbageWinner/epoch_zero_lease` | N-term-winner admits exactly the epoch-zero `zzz` winner; the termination authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n93|| Terminate winner presence | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutWinner/force` | N-term-absent admits exactly the forced winnerless call; the refusal degrades to the malformed-observation class. |\n94|| Terminate force confirmation | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutForce/diagnostics` | N-term-force admits exactly the unforced diagnosed call; the termination authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n95|| Terminate diagnostics | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutDiagnostics/force` | N-term-diag admits exactly the undiagnosed forced call; the termination authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n96|| Terminate session binding | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesForeignSession/prefix_sharing` | N-term-session admits exactly the prefix-sharing foreign target; the refusal degrades to the live-owner class. |\n97|| Terminate live-owner guard | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesLiveOwner/epoch_one` | N-term-live admits exactly the epoch-1 live owner; the epoch-2 owner still refuses. |\n98|| Seal construction census | `TestLeaseTokenConstructorCensus` | T-census-alias adds an alias-backdoor plant preserving `leaseSeal`; the census rejects it while the full suite runs. |\n99|\n100|Crash/idempotency matrix: the gates perform no durable writes, so\n101|there is no crash seam. `TestGatesPerformNoDurableWrites` hashes the\n102|repository tree, evaluates every entry (passing and failing) with\n103|`Bind` and `AuthorizeTerminateStale`, and requires byte-identical\n104|trees and identical verdicts across two runs.\n105|\n106|Refusal classes are proven registered, never invented:\n107|`TestGateRefusalsUseRegisteredCodes` constructs each sentinel through\n108|`internal/axerror` with its exact exit (`lease_conflict`, `not_owner`,\n109|`stale_owner` at 10; `invalid_arguments` at 2;\n110|`local_precondition_failed` at 3), and every park decision unwraps to\n111|its underlying Section 15 cause.\n112|\n113|## Bounds (not silent gaps)\n114|\n115|- No public CLI: 0 of 18 rows are delivered as an `ax` command. The\n116|  shared-library entries above are the deliverable; orchestration\n117|  leaves invoke them.\n118|- No takeover/fork/stop/resume transactions: lifecycle flows are\n119|  modeled as gate callers in `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate`; their\n120|  orchestration belongs to the owning leaves.\n121|- No terminal backend or provider plugin process: the gates own the\n122|  wrapper and provider-operation entry points only.\n123|- No `sessckpt` capture admission to reuse: no such package exists in\n124|  this tree, so `AuthorizeCheckpoint` is the capture admission and its\n125|  tests drive it directly.\n126|- No `resume`, `stop`, `materialize-commit`, or `native-store-plan`\n127|  provider binding: the wire triple is identical, but binding those\n128|  operations here without their callers would be an untestable claim.\n129|- No wall-clock lease expiry and no persisted grants: expiry retires\n130|  only the process-local authorization through the `sessrepo` owner;\n131|  the lease stays authoritative.\n132|- Clause 5.3#5 (`max_observed_epoch + 1`) is caller-side input: the\n133|  store mints head plus one, and the initiator's union maximum arrives\n134|  with the synced store the gate reads.\n135|- Precedence is decided and pinned: malformed calls die first, then\n136|  foreign sessions, then presence and verifiability, then the grant,\n137|  then direction, then the exact tuple match (`TestAuthorizePrecedence`).","final_result":true}}}
